<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Maple Grove &mdash; Standard Detailed Summary</title><style>body{font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;color:#1a1a1a;line-height:1.5;}h1{font-size:16pt;color:#1e3a5f;border-bottom:2pt solid #e8a020;padding-bottom:4pt;margin-bottom:2pt;}h2{font-size:13pt;color:#1e3a5f;margin:14pt 0 4pt;border-bottom:1pt solid #edf0f4;padding-bottom:2pt;}h3{font-size:11.5pt;color:#1e3a5f;margin:11pt 0 3pt;}a{color:#1155cc;text-decoration:underline;}.banner{background:#fff4d6;border:1pt solid #e8a020;color:#7a5b00;font-size:9.5pt;padding:6pt 9pt;margin:0 0 12pt;}.sub{color:#4a5568;font-size:10pt;margin:2pt 0 4pt;}.hdr{font-size:10pt;color:#23344a;margin:1pt 0;}.hdr b{color:#1e3a5f;}.outcome{font-size:12pt;font-weight:bold;color:#14532d;background:#e8f5ec;border-left:3pt solid #1a7a4a;padding:6pt 9pt;margin:8pt 0;}.bottomline{background:#eef3fa;border-left:3pt solid #1e3a5f;padding:6pt 9pt;margin:8pt 0;}ul{margin:4pt 0 8pt 0;}li{margin:2pt 0;}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:10pt;margin:6pt 0;}th,td{border:1pt solid #cdd6e0;padding:4pt 6pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;}th{background:#1e3a5f;color:#fff;font-size:9.5pt;}blockquote{margin:5pt 0 5pt 14pt;padding:3pt 0 3pt 10pt;border-left:2pt solid #cdd6e0;color:#33414f;font-style:italic;}.spk{font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;color:#1e3a5f;}.meta{color:#4a5568;font-size:9pt;border-top:1pt solid #edf0f4;padding-top:6pt;margin-top:18pt;}</style></head><body><h1>Maple Grove &mdash; Standard Detailed Summary</h1><p class="sub">Detailed segment summary &middot; Version 2 of 3 (Standard Detailed)</p><div class="banner"><b>DRAFT — illustrative example.</b> Structure proposal only. Built around a fictional Westfield, IN rezoning hearing to demonstrate the format; figures are not real and are pending validation against the 10-segment research study (see proposal &sect;5). Timestamp links are illustrative.</div><div class="hdr"><b>Project:</b> Maple Grove &mdash; residential PUD subdivision</div><div class="hdr"><b>Jurisdiction / body:</b> City of Westfield, Hamilton County, IN &middot; Advisory Plan Commission</div><div class="hdr"><b>Meeting date:</b> May 19, 2026</div><div class="hdr"><b>Agenda item:</b> Docket 2605-PUD-04 &middot; Ordinance 26-15 (rezone AG-SF1 &rarr; PUD)</div><div class="hdr"><b>Segment:</b> <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1122s">[18:42]</a>&ndash;<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2490s">[41:30]</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1122s">open video at segment start</a></div><h2>Request</h2><p>Arbor Homes LLC (Maple Grove Development Partners), represented by attorney Bill Reardon, requested a rezone of approximately <b>62 acres</b> at the northeast corner of 161st Street and Oak Road from <b>AG-SF1</b> (agricultural / single-family) to a <b>Planned Unit Development (PUD)</b> to permit <b>184 single-family lots</b> with a minimum lot width of 60 ft and roughly 12 acres of HOA-maintained open space. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1215s">[20:15]</a></p><h2>Discussion</h2><h3>Staff report</h3><p>Planning Director Megan Foss summarized the petition and recommended <b>approval subject to conditions</b>, noting density (~3.0 units/acre) is consistent with the comprehensive plan&rsquo;s low-density residential designation. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1122s">[18:42]</a></p><h3>Petitioner presentation</h3><p>Reardon and engineer Priya Nair presented the concept plan, emphasizing the open-space network, a proposed trail stub to the Monon extension, and a price point Arbor positions as attainable move-up product. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1215s">[20:15]</a></p><h3>Commissioner questions &amp; concerns</h3><p>Commissioners pressed on the 161st &amp; Oak intersection capacity and on elementary-school enrollment. Commissioner Marcus Dunn questioned whether a traffic study should precede a favorable recommendation rather than follow it. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1670s">[27:50]</a></p><h3>Public comment</h3><p>Three residents spoke: two opposed (Karen Mills on cut-through traffic; David Cho on school capacity), one in favor (Susan Albright, citing local housing shortage). <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=1990s">[33:10]</a></p><h2>Conditions &amp; commitments</h2><ul><li>Traffic impact study completed before the City Council hearing, with any warranted improvements at 161st &amp; Oak Rd. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2300s">[38:20]</a></li><li>20-ft tree-preservation buffer along the east property line. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2335s">[38:55]</a></li><li>Pedestrian trail connection to the planned Monon extension. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2370s">[39:30]</a></li><li>Minimum 12 acres of open space, HOA-maintained. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2390s">[39:50]</a></li></ul><h2>Motion &amp; vote</h2><p>Commissioner Lena Park moved to forward Docket 2605-PUD-04 to the City Council with a <b>favorable recommendation</b>, subject to the four conditions; seconded by Commissioner Tom Becker. Motion carried <b>6&ndash;1</b> (Whitfield, Ortiz, Park, Becker, Reynolds, Halloran in favor; Dunn opposed). <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2420s">[40:20]</a></p><h2>Outcome &amp; next steps</h2><p>Favorable recommendation forwarded to the <b>Westfield City Council</b>, tentatively scheduled for <b>June 8, 2026</b>. Final rezone requires Council adoption of Ordinance 26-15. <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519&amp;t=2465s">[41:05]</a></p><p class="meta"><b>Sources:</b> <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WF-PC-20260519">Meeting recording (YouTube)</a> &middot; <a href="#">Agenda packet (PDF)</a> &middot; <a href="#">Staff report (PDF)</a><br>Detailed agenda-item summary &mdash; generated from the meeting transcript by MRD (Municipal Resource Dashboard), scoped to this project&rsquo;s agenda item. Timestamp links open the cited moment in the source video.</p></body></html>